          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sound Waves: Characteristics and Applications"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.857,
            0.018,
            0.952,
            0.088
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "N 195"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.088,
            0.776,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this activity, you would have noticed that the frequency is lowest for the ‘Sa’ and gradually increases for the other notes. Each musical note has a distinct frequency, which makes it sound different. You can use the app to compare the frequencies of other sounds, including the voices of your friends too."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.175,
            0.775,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 10.1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If there are 10 density oscillations in 2 seconds at a given position, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "calculate",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the (i) frequency of sound wave, and (ii) its time period."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.227,
            0.742,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "     Frequency of sound "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{wave} = \\frac{\\mathrm{number of oscillations}}{\\mathrm{time taken}} = \\frac{10}{25} = 5\\mathrm{Hz}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.267,
            0.733,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Time taken for a single density oscillation at a position "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2\\mathrm{s}}{10} = 0.2\\mathrm{s}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.302,
            0.393,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pause and Ponder"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.337,
            0.58,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Conduct Activity 10.1 once again with a thick rubber band and then with a thin rubber band. Does the thin rubber band vibrate faster than the thick rubber band? If yes, how do the frequency and time period of the sound produced by the thin rubber band differ from that of the thick rubber band?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.433,
            0.579,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. If the frequency of a sound wave produced by an oscillating piston of a long tube filled with air is 20 Hz, then how many oscillations does the piston complete per minute?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
